{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/202686-kosa-ink-the-lord-provides","id":202686,"title":"KoSA Ink (\"The Lord Provides\")","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-07-19T23:35:11-07:00","id":202686,"title":"KoSA Ink (\"The Lord Provides\")","content":"For The Lord Provides (Mortal Remains p.140), do things like silver rounds count as mundane? Would Holy Water rounds turn to regular water rounds when the original clip's worth runs out, or simply not duplicate at all? How would rounds made of conditional mundane objects (like inherited silver working against Loup-Garou from the Dresden Files; I'm sorry I don't have any WoD examples) affect and be affected by The Lord Provides? Are there any other major things that complicate or are complicated by this Ink?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1963-jet73l","name":"JET73L","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T21:17:01-07:00","id":203467,"title":"","content":"Well, I'd rule it being manufactured ammunition instead. No handloads. Has to be legit purchased rounds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3503-arch-magos","name":"Arch-Magos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T21:49:04-07:00","id":203490,"title":"","content":"You can't exactly wander into the average gun shop and buy silver or blessed rounds, y'know? That's how I read 'mundane.'<br /> <br /> They're bullets. Regular, plain, bullets.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T00:29:53-07:00","id":203591,"title":"","content":"Makes sense. i'm just wondering what counts as &quot;plain&quot;. F'rinstance, lead, no-jacket rounds are about as mundane as you can possibly get, and they're the kind that most people would make themselves, so there's no reason why they shouldn't count even though they're handmade and not manufactured. Maybe none of the bullets are actually fired (and just stay in the clip/chamber), so you can use blessed bullets to fill the clip, it just won't fire blessed bullets unless you switch over to another type of firearm with the same ammunition (a .22 clip-fed pistol as per your Ink to a .22 bolt-action rifle) or deactivate the Ink.<br /> <br /> Following that definition, would The Lord Provides possibly fire silver bullets from a clip full of silver bullets that mysteriously have none of the metaphysical effects of silver, and ONLY the weight and softness (and chemical composition, reflectivity, colour, yadda yadda)? Rather than jamming every time you try to use it with silver (or blessed) bullets? That actually makes sense to me, since there's no such thing as a &quot;regular, plain bullet&quot; (and hey, maybe it would give a hunter with The Lord Provides a DISadvantage if he or she is pitted against something that's weak against lead and the usual hailstorm of lead bullets doesn't set off its weakness).<br /> <br /> Edit: Arch-Magos: Oh, did you mean make it a pure GM fiat that the bullets have to be mass-produced (presumably by mundane means)? Reasonable. Reasonable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1963,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1963-jet73l","user":"JET73L","date":". 07-21-2014, 04:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1963-jet73l","name":"JET73L","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T07:21:10-07:00","id":203825,"title":"","content":"On the other hand, there's nothing preventing you from getting an Ink of, say, a bazooka.<br /> <br /> The problem is procuring one, and keeping it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T18:59:22-07:00","id":204522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JET73L</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/202686-kosa-ink-the-lord-provides?p=203591#post203591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Makes sense. i'm just wondering what counts as &amp;quot;plain&amp;quot;. F'rinstance, lead, no-jacket rounds are about as mundane as you can possibly get, and they're the kind that most people would make themselves, so there's no reason why they shouldn't count even though they're handmade and not manufactured. Maybe none of the bullets are actually fired (and just stay in the clip/chamber), so you can use blessed bullets to fill the clip, it just won't fire blessed bullets unless you switch over to another type of firearm with the same ammunition (a .22 clip-fed pistol as per your Ink to a .22 bolt-action rifle) or deactivate the Ink.<br /> <br /> Following that definition, would The Lord Provides possibly fire silver bullets from a clip full of silver bullets that mysteriously have none of the metaphysical effects of silver, and ONLY the weight and softness (and chemical composition, reflectivity, colour, yadda yadda)? Rather than jamming every time you try to use it with silver (or blessed) bullets? That actually makes sense to me, since there's no such thing as a &amp;quot;regular, plain bullet&amp;quot; (and hey, maybe it would give a hunter with The Lord Provides a DISadvantage if he or she is pitted against something that's weak against lead and the usual hailstorm of lead bullets doesn't set off its weakness).<br /> <br /> Edit: Arch-Magos: Oh, did you mean make it a pure GM fiat that the bullets have to be mass-produced (presumably by mundane means)? Reasonable. Reasonable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically, what I mean is they have to be something you could find at a wal-mart. Hollowpoints are fine, something like Dragon's Breath or explosive rounds is not. It makes you like Arnold from Commando, not like some FPS protagonist with infinite ammo on. That's how I'd rule it to prevent some smartass player trying to do something like a fully auto grenade launcher. That's not to say that stuff like going Rambo with an M60 isn't possible, but you still have to deal with recoil and jams.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3503-arch-magos","name":"Arch-Magos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T19:12:28-07:00","id":204526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/202686-kosa-ink-the-lord-provides?p=203490#post203490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can't exactly wander into the average gun shop and buy silver or blessed rounds, y'know? That's how I read 'mundane.'<br /> <br /> They're bullets. Regular, plain, bullets.</div> </div> </div> </div>A slight counter to this is that it works on all sorts of explosive rounds that the average civilians couldn't get either. It won't replicate compound rounds from Mortal Remains, but load in two smart grenade rounds into your AA-12 and you'll be shooting pretty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T00:54:12-07:00","id":204781,"title":"","content":"I've always read it as the average munition fired from that type of weapon. Shotguns fire .00 buck shot, 9mm fire full metal jacket rounds, grenade launchers fire your typical fragmentation grenade. You can't get Dragon's breath shotgun shells, incendiary grenades or high explosive rounds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2861-nyx","name":"Nyx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2861_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T08:33:50-07:00","id":204980,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/122598-mortal-remains-is-here?p=123001#post123001\">I asked David Hill about it when Mortal Remains came out</a>. If it's not a really weird shot(like an Endowment), and you can fire off two of them in a row, it works.<br /> <br /> So again, an AA-12 with high explosive rounds(the veryexample I used when I asked) can turn into an unending stream of explosions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 07-22-2014, 11:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T08:45:59-07:00","id":204992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/202686-kosa-ink-the-lord-provides?p=204980#post204980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/122598-mortal-remains-is-here?p=123001#post123001&amp;quot;]I</a> asked David Hill about it when Mortal Remains came out[/URL]. If it's not a really weird shot(like an Endowment), and you can fire off two of them in a row, it works.<br /> <br /> So again, an AA-12 with high explosive rounds(the veryexample I used when I asked) can turn into an unending stream of explosions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hahaha holy crap. That's amazingly good for an endowment. I'd still try and stop the explosive rounds shenanigans as a GM, but that's just good to know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3503-arch-magos","name":"Arch-Magos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}